    "information": {
      "description": "<p><em>Named for the barge haulers of the Volga, and it means it. Techtronika built this for dock unions and reconstruction crews after the Unification War: cheap Neo-Soviet arms, tools for hands, and nothing else. It's the cheapest way to go metal that isn't a crime. *Treat as Expensive for availability.</em></p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> 9,400eb (Expensive*)<br><strong>Humanity Loss:</strong> 19 (6d6)<br><strong>Frame:</strong> Sigma (12): BODY 12<br><strong>Eyes:</strong> Cybereye ×2<br><strong>Base chrome (no HL):</strong> Discount Cyberaudio Suite and Neo-Soviet Cyberarm ×2 (replace the standard parts)<br><strong>Chrome:</strong> Grip Foot ×2, Skin Weave, Tool Hand ×2</p><p>Every body includes the standard chassis (Cyberarm ×2, Cyberaudio Suite, Cyberleg ×2, Cyberskull, an Internal Linear Frame and a Neuroport) at no HL, plus its eyes and base chrome. Going metal needs a Biosystem (bought separately) and a Hospital.</p><p><small>Item Compendium (2070) • Full Body Conversions</small></p>",
      "alias": "",
      "history": "",
      "notes": ""
    }
  },
